  "tours": [
    {
      "id": "tour:parse-errors",
      "title": "How Zod returns parsed data or validation errors",
      "summary": "Zod schemas offer a throwing parse and a safe result for validation. Both run the schema and inspect its issue list. Invalid input makes the throwing path construct and throw an error; the safe path returns `success: false`. The safe result builds its error when a caller reads that property.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "t1",
          "view": "view:outcome",
          "focus": [
            "outcome:1"
          ],
          "note": "### The caller chooses the error contract\n\nA schema exposes a method that throws and one that returns a result object. Both send the input to the parser.",
          "code": [
            {
              "file": "packages/zod/src/v4/classic/schemas.ts",
              "find": "return parse.parse(this, data, params, { callee: _parse });",
              "role": "call-site"
            },
            {
              "file": "packages/zod/src/v4/classic/schemas.ts",
              "find": "return parse.safeParse(this, data, params);",
              "role": "call-site"
            }
          ],
          "editor": {
            "primary": "packages/zod/src/v4/classic/schemas.ts"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "t2",
          "view": "view:outcome",
          "focus": [
            "outcome:2"
          ],
          "note": "### Both choices run validation and inspect issues\n\nThe core parser executes the schema with an empty issue list. Any collected issue marks the input invalid.",
          "code": [
            {
              "file": "packages/zod/src/v4/core/parse.ts",
              "symbol": "_parse",
              "find": "const result = schema._zod.run({ value, issues: [] }, ctx);",
              "role": "definition"
            },
            {
              "file": "packages/zod/src/v4/core/parse.ts",
              "symbol": "_safeParse",
              "find": "const result = schema._zod.run({ value, issues: [] }, ctx);",
              "role": "definition"
            }
          ],
          "editor": {
            "primary": "packages/zod/src/v4/core/parse.ts"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "t3",
          "view": "view:outcome",
          "focus": [
            "outcome:3"
          ],
          "note": "### A valid input returns parsed data\n\nThe safe path wraps parsed data with `success: true`. The throwing path returns the parsed value directly.",
          "code": [
            {
              "file": "packages/zod/src/v4/core/parse.ts",
              "symbol": "_safeParse",
              "find": "({ success: true, data: result.value } as any)",
              "role": "definition"
            },
            {
              "file": "packages/zod/src/v4/core/parse.ts",
              "symbol": "_parse",
              "find": "return result.value as core.output<typeof schema>;",
              "role": "definition"
            }
          ],
          "editor": {
            "primary": "packages/zod/src/v4/core/parse.ts"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "t4",
          "view": "view:outcome",
          "focus": [
            "outcome:4"
          ],
          "note": "### Invalid input has two different outcomes\n\nThe throwing path finalizes issues and throws an error. The safe path returns `success: false` and keeps error creation deferred.",
          "code": [
            {
              "file": "packages/zod/src/v4/core/parse.ts",
              "symbol": "_parse",
              "find": "throw e;",
              "role": "definition"
            },
            {
              "file": "packages/zod/src/v4/core/parse.ts",
              "symbol": "_safeParse",
              "find": "failure(_Err, result.issues, ctx)",
              "role": "definition"
            }
          ],
          "editor": {
            "primary": "packages/zod/src/v4/core/parse.ts"
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "t5",
          "view": "view:outcome",
          "focus": [
            "outcome:6"
          ],
          "note": "### The first error read constructs the error\n\nA caller can branch on `success` without building the error. Reading `error` finalizes issues once and caches the instance.",
          "code": [
            {
              "file": "packages/zod/src/v4/core/parse.ts",
              "symbol": "failure",
              "find": "get error() {",
              "role": "definition"
            },
            {
              "file": "packages/zod/src/v4/core/parse.ts",
              "symbol": "failure",
              "find": "error = new Err(issues.map((iss) => util.finalizeIssue(iss, ctx, core.config())));",
              "role": "definition"
            }
          ],
          "editor": {
            "primary": "packages/zod/src/v4/core/parse.ts"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
